            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0212" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.00101/66</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minutes of the Daily Meetings of the Commissioners
                        Plenipotentiary, Thursday, May 8th, 1919</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1919-05-08">May 8, 1919</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <item>Present: <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Lansing</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. White</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">General Bliss</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Herter</hi></item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
                <pb facs="0213" n="177" xml:id="pg177"/>
                <p>1. Memorandum No. 266 addressed to General Bliss regarding dinner to the Foreign
                    Representatives on the Joint Secretariat written by Colonel U. S. Grant was
                    considered by the Commissioners. They decided that it would be most desirable
                    for Colonel Grant to give the dinner which he suggests and left the question of
                    expenses to his discretion. <seg type="margin">Dinner to Joint Secretariat by
                        Col. Grant</seg></p>
            </div>
        </body>
